1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,300
A handful of wool is mostly air.

2
00:00:03,550 --> 00:00:05,850
A felting needle changes that.

3
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:08,780
Its tiny barbs catch a few fibres on every poke,

4
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:11,900
and drag them in, where they tangle and stay.

5
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,600
Forty pokes, and the cloud is a ball.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,300
Four hundred, and it holds its shape.

7
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,900
A second ball becomes a head.

8
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,700
A cone becomes a beak.

9
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,400
The wings are flat layers, pressed on.

10
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:30,300
Colour goes in the same way.

11
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,000
Where two shades meet, the needle blends them, and there is no edge.

12
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,000
Last, two small eyes.

13
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:46,300
Four thousand pokes. And what was air is looking back.
